{
  "email": "hannah.lee@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender reports temporary password rejected and password change at sign-in fails with error; checking account status and must_change_password per KB-003."
}

{
  "user_id": 12,
  "reason": "Reviewing recent sign-in attempts to see where and how the failed password-change attempts originated (KB-003 quick check, KB-001 network check)."
}

{
  "user_id": 12,
  "reason": "Checking MFA enrollment, since a new hire may need MFA set up before the password change completes."
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0112",
  "reason": "Checking whether her assigned laptop is online and healthy, since KB-003 says the password change works best on the laptop sign-in screen while on the office network or VPN."
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, thanks for the details. Your account is active and not locked, and it's set to require a new password at your next sign-in, so the temporary password itself was accepted. The error is most likely caused by where the change is being made. Please try this: on your laptop (BL-LT-0112), sign in from the Windows sign-in screen, not a web page, while connected to the office network or the company VPN. When it asks you to change your password, enter the temporary password, then choose a new one that is at least 14 characters and different from any recent password. Check that Caps Lock is off and that you're not mixing up l/I or 0/O. If you still get an error, please reply with the exact wording of the message, whether you're on the laptop or a web page, and whether you're on the office network or VPN, and we'll take the next step.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user: account active, sign_in_blocked false, failed_login_count 0, must_change_password true, password_last_set 2026-10-11 03:28 UTC, VPN enabled. Sign-in logs: 10 successful sign-ins from corporate and residential networks, 0 failed password, 0 MFA denials, no hosting or foreign locations. Possible inconsistency: logs show successful sign-ins from 09-28 to 10-09, which predate the password_last_set date and do not fit a day-one new hire. Verify whether this is a rehire or a reused account record. MFA: not enrolled (enrolled false), which may matter if the change flow requires MFA; unverified. Device BL-LT-0112 online, last check-in 2026-10-11 03:16 UTC, 130 GB free, no warnings. No lockout, so no unlock or reset requested. Next step: get exact error text and sign-in path from user. If the error persists on the laptop while on network/VPN, consider KB-002 reissue or escalate to Tier 2 for the change-flow error and the MFA enrollment question. KB-001 not applicable (no lockout).",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-003"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
